hadiths[23]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1287","It is narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Musa al-Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Whoever takes up weapons against us is not from among us.\""\nAl-Adab Al-Mufrad Hadith: 1287 Arabic Hadith: 1287"""
"1288","It is narrated by the Companion of the Messenger, Abu 'Azah Yasar ibn 'Abd (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When Allah"," the Most High"," wills for a servant to die in a certain land"," He places for him some occupation in that place.\""\nAl-Adab Al-Mufrad Hadith: 1288 Arabic Hadith: 1288"""
"1289","It is narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he wiped his nose with a cloth and then said: \Woe"," woe! Abu Hurayrah wipes his nose with cloth! I have found myself in a state of fainting between the chamber of Sayyidah A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) and the pulpit"," due to hunger. The people (upon seeing this) would say: 'He is mad!' whereas nothing afflicted me except hunger.\""\nAl-Adab Al-Mufrad Hadith: 1289 Arabic Hadith: 1289"""
"1290","It is narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: \O Messenger of Allah! We find in our hearts such whisperings that we would never utter them even if we were to be given all the wealth of the earth.\"" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Did you find such a thing in your hearts?\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""That is the clear and pure faith (iman).\""\nAl-Adab Al-Mufrad Hadith: 1290 Arabic Hadith: 1290"""
"1291","It is narrated by Shahr ibn Hawshab (may Allah have mercy on him) that I and my maternal uncle went to Sayyidah A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) and said: \One of us finds in his breast such thoughts that if he were to express them"," his Hereafter would be ruined"," and if they were to become apparent"," he would be killed.\"" She said that upon hearing this"," she said 'Allahu Akbar' three times and said: \""This was asked of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)"," and he said: 'When such a situation befalls any one of you"," let him say Allahu Akbar three times. Indeed"," this awareness (of such whisperings) is not felt by anyone except a believer (mu'min).'\""\nAl-Adab Al-Mufrad Hadith: 1291 Arabic Hadith: 1291"""
"1292","It is narrated by Sayyiduna Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \People will continue to ask about things that are not going to happen"," until they will say: 'Allah is the Creator of all things"," so who created Allah?'\""\nAl-Adab Al-Mufrad Hadith: 1292 Arabic Hadith: 1292"""
"1293","It is narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Beware of suspicion (su' al-zann)"," for suspicion is the most false of speech. Do not spy on one another"," and do not compete with one another in worldly matters. Do not turn your backs on one another"," and do not envy one another"," and do not harbour hatred for one another. And be"," O servants of Allah"," brothers.\""\nAl-Adab Al-Mufrad Hadith: 1293 Arabic Hadith: 1293"""
"1294","It is narrated by Sayyiduna Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with one of his wives when a man passed by. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and said: \O so-and-so! This is my wife"," so-and-so.\"" The man said: \""I may suspect others"," but I cannot suspect you.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Indeed"," Satan flows through the veins of the son of Adam like blood.\""\nAl-Adab Al-Mufrad Hadith: 1294 Arabic Hadith: 1294"""
"1295","It is narrated by Sayyiduna 'Abdullah ibn 'Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) that the one whose property has been stolen continues to suspect others until he surpasses even the thief (in sin).\\nAl-Adab Al-Mufrad Hadith: 1295 Arabic Hadith: 1295"""
"1296","It is narrated from Bilāl bin Sa'd al-Ash'arī (may Allah have mercy on him) that Mu'āwiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote to Abū al-Dardā' (may Allah be pleased with him): \Write to me the names of the wicked (fāsiq) people of Damascus.\"" He replied: \""What concern do I have with the wicked of Damascus? How would I know them?\"" His son Bilāl (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""I shall write their names for you.\"" So he wrote their names. Abū al-Dardā' (may Allah be pleased with him) asked: \""How did you come to know about them? How did you find out that they are wicked"," unless you are one of them? Therefore"," write your own name first.\"" And so he wrote the names but did not send them.\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 1296*"""
"1297","It is narrated from 'Abd al-'Azīz bin Qays (may Allah have mercy on him) that I came to 'Abdullāh bin 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) while a slave-girl was trimming his hair. He said: \The powder or lotion used for removing hair softens the skin.\""\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 1297*"""
"1298","It is narrated from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Five things are from among the acts of natural disposition (fiṭrah): circumcision"," shaving the pubic hair"," plucking the armpit hair"," trimming the moustache"," and cutting the nails.\""\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 1298*"""
"1299","It is narrated from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Five things are from among the acts of natural disposition (fiṭrah): circumcision"," shaving the pubic hair"," cutting the nails"," plucking the armpit hair"," and trimming the moustache.\""\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 1299*"""
"1300","It is narrated from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \Five things are from among the acts of natural disposition (fiṭrah): cutting the nails"," trimming the moustache"," plucking the armpit hair"," shaving the pubic hair"," and circumcision.\""\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 1300*"""
"1301","It is narrated from Abū Ṭufayl (may Allah be pleased with him) that I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributing meat at the place of al-Ji'rānah, and at that time I was a young boy of nine years. I was picking up pieces of camel meat when a woman came to him, and he spread his cloak for her. I asked: \Who is this?\"" It was said: \""This is the woman who nursed you"," your (foster) mother.\""\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 1301*"""
"1302","It is narrated from al-Mughīrah bin Shu'bah (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man said: \May Allah reform the commander! Indeed"," your gatekeeper gives preference in granting permission to those whom he recognizes.\"" He said: \""May Allah accept his excuse. Indeed"," recognition (of those known) is beneficial even at the place of a biting dog or a charging camel (meaning that because of this"," the gatekeeper does not allow strangers who might cause harm to approach those who are close and known).\""\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 1302*"""
"1303","It is narrated from Ibrāhīm al-Nakha'ī (may Allah have mercy on him), who said: \Our companions used to permit us every form of play except (playing with) dogs.\"" Abū 'Abdullāh"," Imam al-Bukhārī (may Allah have mercy on him)"," said: \""That is"," (they permitted) children.\""\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 1303*"""
"1304","It is narrated from 'Abd al-'Azīz (may Allah have mercy on him) that a righteous elder known as Abū 'Uqbah informed me: \Once I passed along a road with Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both)"," and they passed by some Ethiopian children who were playing. He took out two dirhams and gave them to them.\""\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 1304*"""
"1305","It is narrated from 'Ā'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to send my friends to me, and they would play with me with dolls.\\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 1305*"""
"1306","It is narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a person chasing a pigeon. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \He is a devil chasing a she-devil.\""\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 1306 | Arabic Hadith: 1306"""
"1307","It is narrated by Sayyiduna al-Hasan al-Basri (may Allah have mercy on him) that he said: Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) would invariably command in every blessed Jumu'ah sermon that dogs be killed and pigeons be slaughtered.\nThrough another chain of narration, it is narrated from al-Hasan al-Basri (may Allah have mercy on him) himself that Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) used to command in his sermon the killing of dogs and the slaughtering of pigeons.\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad, Hadith: 1307 | Arabic Hadith: 1307"
"1308","It is narrated by Sayyiduna Zayd ibn Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) that one day Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) came to his house and sought permission to enter. He (Zayd) granted him permission to enter, while his head was in the hands of a slave-girl who was combing it. He wished to remove his head from the slave-girl, but Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Let her finish combing it.\"" He submitted: \""O Commander of the Faithful"," you could have sent me a message and I would have come to you.\"" Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""The matter was mine (and therefore it was more fitting that I should come myself).\""\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 1308 | Arabic Hadith: 1308"""
"1309","It is narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: When a person spits phlegm in front of people, he should conceal it with both his palms until his phlegm falls to the ground. And when a person is fasting, he should apply oil so that the effect of fasting is not visible upon him.\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad, Hadith: 1309 | Arabic Hadith: 1309"
